            {
              "id": "blk-regla-recurrencia-base-general",
              "type": "note",
              "variant": "warning",
              "title": "Rule",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "blk-regla-recurrencia-base-general-texto",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every recurrence equation MUST have a general case AND a base case. Without base case there is no stop. The base case always has constant cost:"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "inlineMath",
                      "latex": "T(0)=c"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ","
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "inlineMath",
                      "latex": "T(1)=c"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sectionId": "sec-recursion-cola",
          "slug": "recursion-cola",
          "title": "11.6 Tail recursion",
          "order": 7,
          "kind": "theory",
          "trackProgress": true,
          "estimatedMinutes": 3,
          "learningObjectives": [
            {
              "objectiveId": "definir-recursion-cola",
              "text": "Deende when a recursion is tail recursion."
            },
            {
              "objectiveId": "explicar-conversion-iterativa",
              "text": "Explain why a tail recursion can become an iteration."
            },
            {
              "objectiveId": "comparar-espacio-recursion-iteracion",
              "text": "Compare the space cost of the recursive version and the equivalent iterative version."
            }
          ],
          "prerequisites": {
            "modules": [],
            "sections": [
              {
                "id": "sec-ambientes-ejecucion-pila",
                "kind": "required"
              },
              {
                "id": "sec-estructura-algoritmo-recursivo",
                "kind": "required"
              }
            ]
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "blk-recursion-cola-definicion",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A recursion is tail recursion when the recursive call is the last thing that happens in the general case. In that case, the system can convert it to an iteration automatically or manually because there is nothing pending after the call."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "blk-recursion-cola-clave",
              "type": "note",
              "variant": "success",
              "title": "Key",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "blk-recursion-cola-clave-texto",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "If a recursive algorithm is tail-based, it is always advisable to convert it to iterative: same logic, space cost"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "inlineMath",
                      "latex": "O(1)"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "instead of"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "inlineMath",
                      "latex": "O(n)"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "by the stack."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
